      "math_academy_id": "q-10204",
      "sequence_position": 6,
      "problem": "Solve the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned} & x+2y-z=10 \\\\  & y+5z=15 \\\\  & -z=5\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "worked_solution": "The third equation states that \n\n$$\n-z=5\\,⟹\\,z=-5.\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into the second equation, we get\n\n$$\ny+5(-5)=15\\,⟹\\,y=15+25=40.\n$$\n\nNow, we substitute $z=-5$ and $y=40$ into the first equation to get\n\n$$\nx+2(40)-(-5)=10\\,⟹\\,x=10-80-5=-75.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x=-75,y=40$ and $z=-5.$ In vector form, the solution can be written as $⟨-75,40,-5⟩.$",
